title: General Müller's Orders
subtitle: The Reichswehr bans the hundreds in Saxony.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_october = 1 and crisis_time >= 1 and e23_rising_phase = 0 and e23_muller_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.octTick(Q.crisis_time);
RG.district('saxony', {repression: 15});
RG.district('thuringia', {repression: 8});
RG.news('General Müller bans the hundreds in Saxony', 3);
Q.e23_muller_done = 1;
!}

= General Müller's Orders

On 13 October General Alfred Müller bans the proletarian hundreds and puts the Saxon police under his own command. Reichswehr battalions from Bavaria, Württemberg and Prussia start arriving by train at Leipzig and Dresden. [? if saxony_government = 1 : Our ministers are ordered to stop inciting the population. ?] In Berlin the cabinet is preparing a Reichsexekution, the Reich's power to depose a state government.

His patrols have orders to search the allotments and the cellars.

- @defy: March the hundreds through Chemnitz.
- @hide: Obey, and hide the rifles.
- @appeal: Appeal to the Social Democratic workers to defend their government.
- @now: Strike first, this week.

@defy
subtitle: The workers see our strength. The soldiers find some of the rifles.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 8, repression: 5});
Q.e23_oct_hall += 6;
Q.e23_oct_arms = Math.max(0, Q.e23_oct_arms - 2);
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

Twenty thousand of the hundreds march through Chemnitz on Sunday. The Reichswehr watches from the pavements, and in the evening its patrols dig up two of the caches they saw being visited.

@hide
subtitle: The rifles will be there when they are needed. The workers wonder what we are waiting for.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_arms_hidden = 1;
Q.e23_oct_hall -= 3;
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

The hundreds become football clubs again. Their rifles go into cellars, under the coal.

@appeal
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The SPD branches in Leipzig and Dresden are angry too.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any appeal to the SPD.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e23_oct_hall += (Q.spd_relation >= 25 ? 9 : 4);
Q.spd_relation += 4;
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

SPD branches in Leipzig and Dresden pass resolutions for a general strike if the Reichswehr touches the Saxon government. Their executive in Berlin passes nothing.

@now
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Surprise, without the preparations. Fischer's people want it.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('uprising');
RG.news('The rising begins a week early', 3);
RG.e22.octRise(['saxony', 'thuringia', 'berlin'], 'The German Revolution', 'Hold the districts that have risen until the Reichswehr breaks.', -3);
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

The signal goes out a week early. In Saxony, Thuringia and Berlin the hundreds take the town halls and the stations, and couriers race to the districts that were not ready.
